I have a vote on the difficulty side. I can win without too much
difficulty in 2.1, and the game is now that much less interesting.
Perhaps even if the general difficulty level is not increased, some
particular type of total winner status might be made more difficult,
maybe reserving some special monsters (the wizard is still a wimp, and
demon lords are not a serious problem) and/or environments for the
endgame. However I am against increasing difficulty by weakening the
player -- if anything the player should have even more potential
for godly powers, so long as the game eventually gets hard enough to
make playing a challenge.

